  "tool_gate_cases": {
    "desc": "Tool-aware taint gate: (tool_name, taint_state, action, destructive set) -> decision, pinned identically in both SDKs (TS evaluateToolTaintGate, Python evaluate_tool_taint_gate). The composition this pins: a tainted session under the DEFAULT flag action still has its calls to tools in the destructive-capability set REFUSED - detection quality is not the lever, reachability is. A missed injection is harmless if it cannot reach send_money, and a detected one no longer bricks the session (ordinary egress stays flagged) while the dangerous capabilities go dark. Membership in the operator's set is EXACT tool names - a set that pattern-matched would be a detector again. The set is the UNION of that list and `declared_destructive`, the tool descriptor's own annotations.destructiveHint resolved at discovery, so a deployment that configured nothing still gets a capability gate. Both sources are add-only, which is why `destructive_source` names which one decided. `destructive: true` marks a block that came from the set rather than a blanket block action.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "id": "untainted_destructive_tool_runs",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tainted": false,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "destructive_tools": [
            "send_money"
          ]
        },
        "tool_name": "send_money",
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "none"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tainted_flag_nondestructive_flags",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "destructive_tools": [
            "send_money"
          ]
        },
        "tool_name": "read_file",
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "flag"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tainted_flag_destructive_blocks",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "THE case: flag mode, and the destructive capability is still refused",
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "destructive_tools": [
            "send_money"
          ]
        },
        "tool_name": "send_money",
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "block",
          "destructive": true,
          "destructive_source": "operator"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tainted_block_mode_blocks_everything",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "block",
          "destructive_tools": []
        },
        "tool_name": "read_file",
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "block"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "empty_set_flag_stays_flag",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "destructive_tools": []
        },
        "tool_name": "send_money",
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "flag"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "membership_is_exact_names_only",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "send_money_v2 is not send_money: no prefix or pattern matching, ever",
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "destructive_tools": [
            "send_money"
          ]
        },
        "tool_name": "send_money_v2",
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "flag"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "disabled_latch_never_gates",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tainted": true,
        "config": null,
        "tool_name": "send_money",
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "none"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "hinted_destructive_blocks_with_no_operator_list",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "The default case this exists for: the operator configured no destructive_tools at all, and the tool's own descriptor declared it destructive. A tainted session loses it anyway.",
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag"
        },
        "tool_name": "delete_row",
        "declared_destructive": true,
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "block",
          "destructive": true,
          "destructive_source": "descriptor_hint"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "unhinted_tool_with_no_operator_list_only_flags",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "An ABSENT hint means non-destructive. Stated rather than implied: most deployed servers publish no annotations, and reading silence as destructive would turn flag mode into a blanket block for them.",
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag"
        },
        "tool_name": "read_file",
        "declared_destructive": false,
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "flag"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "operator_entry_wins_over_a_descriptor_claiming_safety",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "The server must not be able to talk its way OUT. A tool the operator listed is destructive even when its descriptor declares no hint (which is how a `destructiveHint: false` descriptor reaches this function - a false hint resolves to declared_destructive false, contributing nothing).",
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "destructive_tools": [
            "send_money"
          ]
        },
        "tool_name": "send_money",
        "declared_destructive": false,
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "block",
          "destructive": true,
          "destructive_source": "operator"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "operator_source_wins_when_both_sources_agree",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "Both sources name the tool. The verdict is the same block; the attribution reports the operator, because that is the fact an auditor can act on without trusting the server.",
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "destructive_tools": [
            "send_money"
          ]
        },
        "tool_name": "send_money",
        "declared_destructive": true,
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "block",
          "destructive": true,
          "destructive_source": "operator"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "hints_ignored_when_the_operator_turns_them_off",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "honor_destructive_hints false restricts the set to the operator's list alone. Because the hint can only ever ADD, turning it off never tightens anything - it exists for an operator who wants the set to be exactly what their config says.",
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "honor_destructive_hints": false
        },
        "tool_name": "delete_row",
        "declared_destructive": true,
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "flag"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "hints_off_still_honors_the_operator_list",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tainted": true,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag",
          "honor_destructive_hints": false,
          "destructive_tools": [
            "delete_row"
          ]
        },
        "tool_name": "delete_row",
        "declared_destructive": true,
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "block",
          "destructive": true,
          "destructive_source": "operator"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "untainted_hinted_tool_runs",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "The capability set gates a COMPROMISED session, not every session. An untainted caller reaches a hinted-destructive tool normally.",
        "tainted": false,
        "config": {
          "enabled": true,
          "action": "flag"
        },
        "tool_name": "delete_row",
        "declared_destructive": true,
        "expect": {
          "enforcement": "none"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "descriptor_hint_cases": {
    "desc": "declaresDestructive / declares_destructive: reading annotations.destructiveHint off a tool descriptor. ONE-DIRECTIONAL by design - only an affirmative `true` counts. The descriptor is authored by the tool server, which is the party the taint latch defends against, so a `false` and an absent hint are the same thing here: neither is evidence of safety worth acting on, and honoring `false` would let a hostile server leave the destructive set by writing one word about itself. Reading is strict equality, not truthiness, so the table is exactly expressible and identical in both languages; a server wanting out can just omit the field, so strictness costs nothing. NOTE this deliberately differs from MCP's own reading of the field, where an unspecified destructiveHint is treated as true - that default only works if `false` is honored, and here it must not be.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "id": "explicit_true_declares",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tool": {
          "name": "delete_row",
          "annotations": {
            "destructiveHint": true
          }
        },
        "expect": true
      },
      {
        "id": "explicit_false_declares_nothing",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tool": {
          "name": "read_file",
          "annotations": {
            "destructiveHint": false
          }
        },
        "expect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "absent_hint_declares_nothing",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tool": {
          "name": "read_file",
          "annotations": {
            "readOnlyHint": true
          }
        },
        "expect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "absent_annotations_declare_nothing",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tool": {
          "name": "read_file"
        },
        "expect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "null_annotations_declare_nothing",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tool": {
          "name": "read_file",
          "annotations": null
        },
        "expect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "string_true_is_not_true",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "Strict equality: a string is not the boolean. A server that wanted the tool in the set could simply send the boolean.",
        "tool": {
          "name": "t",
          "annotations": {
            "destructiveHint": "true"
          }
        },
        "expect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "number_one_is_not_true",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tool": {
          "name": "t",
          "annotations": {
            "destructiveHint": 1
          }
        },
        "expect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "array_annotations_declare_nothing",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "A non-object annotations value is not a mapping and carries no hint.",
        "tool": {
          "name": "t",
          "annotations": [
            {
              "destructiveHint": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "expect": false
      },
      {
        "id": "read_only_hint_cannot_de_escalate",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "desc": "readOnlyHint is a SAFETY claim from the untrusted author, so it is not read at all - it could only ever remove.",
        "tool": {
          "name": "t",
          "annotations": {
            "readOnlyHint": true,
            "destructiveHint": true
          }
        },
        "expect": true
      },
      {
        "id": "null_tool_declares_nothing",
        "sdk_support": {
          "ts": "required",
          "py": "required"
        },
        "tool": null,
        "expect": false
      }
    ]
  }
}
